      "id": 164198,
      "name": "Spiff",
      "username": "Spiff",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/spiff/{size}/1865_2.png",
      "created_at": "2016-03-01T22:19:59.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>One thing I can't figure out is why the planets aren't round. &nbsp;The best I can figure is that it's to make clear what the planet's orientation should be when lining it up, but planets are round. &nbsp;There has to be a better way to handle that.</p><p>Also, euro-blocks are cool and everything, but there's no way I'm playing a game like this, where you're adding life to planets and evolving them, without alien-shaped tokens to represent that, even if I have to make something myself. &nbsp;Blocks and cylinders are far too dry for this Ameritrasher.</p>",
      "post_number": 10,
      "post_type": 1,
